1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:16,283
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June twentieth. China is limiting exports of a metal called tungsten, and that's a worry for Japanese makers of phones and chips. Let's listen.

2
00:00:16,884 --> 00:00:19,643
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:20,344 --> 00:00:29,440
[News] 中国が、「タングステン」という金属を、外国に売るのを制限すると発表しました。

4
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:36,692
[News] タングステンは、とてもかたくて、熱につよい金属です。

5
00:00:37,392 --> 00:00:45,072
[News] スマートフォンや、半導体や、工場の道具を作るときに使います。

6
00:00:45,771 --> 00:00:51,963
[News] 世界のタングステンの多くは、中国で作られています。

7
00:00:52,664 --> 00:01:00,655
[News] だから、中国がこの金属を売らないと、ほかの国はとても困ります。

8
00:01:01,356 --> 00:01:08,099
[News] 日本の会社も、タングステンの多くを中国から買っています。

9
00:01:08,799 --> 00:01:16,024
[News] 今、日本の会社は、ほかの国から買う方法を探しています。

10
00:01:16,724 --> 00:01:23,540
[News] 同じ金属を、何度も使えるようにする研究も進んでいます。

11
00:01:24,239 --> 00:01:32,135
[News] 大切な金属を安定して手に入れることが、これからの大きな課題です。

12
00:01:32,835 --> 00:01:34,468
[Host] Let's break it down.

13
00:01:35,067 --> 00:01:45,459
[Slow] 中国が、「タングステン」という金属を、外国に売るのを制限すると発表しました。

14
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:51,587
[Host] China announced it will restrict selling a metal called tungsten to other countries.

15
00:01:52,188 --> 00:01:54,563
[Vocab] 金属

16
00:01:54,963 --> 00:02:01,995
[Host] It means metal — iron, gold, copper, and so on. Tungsten is one kind of metal.

17
00:02:02,596 --> 00:02:10,084
[Slow] タングステンは、とてもかたくて、熱につよい金属です。

18
00:02:10,883 --> 00:02:14,891
[Host] Tungsten is a very hard metal that stands up well to heat.

19
00:02:15,491 --> 00:02:17,580
[Vocab] 熱

20
00:02:17,979 --> 00:02:24,508
[Host] It means heat. The same word also means a fever when you're sick. Here, resistant to heat.

21
00:02:25,108 --> 00:02:33,891
[Slow] スマートフォンや、半導体や、工場の道具を作るときに使います。

22
00:02:34,692 --> 00:02:39,852
[Host] It's used to make things like smartphones, semiconductors, and factory tools.

23
00:02:40,451 --> 00:02:42,611
[Vocab] 道具

24
00:02:43,012 --> 00:02:49,852
[Host] It means a tool or instrument. Cooking tools, factory tools — the all-purpose word for tools.

25
00:02:50,451 --> 00:02:57,532
[Slow] 世界のタングステンの多くは、中国で作られています。

26
00:02:58,331 --> 00:03:01,524
[Host] Much of the world's tungsten is made in China.

27
00:03:02,123 --> 00:03:04,355
[Vocab] 世界

28
00:03:04,756 --> 00:03:10,132
[Host] It means the world. A related word means the whole world over, everywhere.

29
00:03:10,731 --> 00:03:19,852
[Slow] だから、中国がこの金属を売らないと、ほかの国はとても困ります。

30
00:03:20,651 --> 00:03:25,259
[Host] So if China doesn't sell this metal, other countries are in real trouble.

31
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:27,948
[Vocab] 困る

32
00:03:28,348 --> 00:03:35,572
[Host] It means to be in trouble, to be at a loss, or stuck about what to do. A very useful everyday verb.

33
00:03:36,171 --> 00:03:43,876
[Slow] 日本の会社も、タングステンの多くを中国から買っています。

34
00:03:44,675 --> 00:03:49,427
[Host] Japanese companies, too, buy much of their tungsten from China.

35
00:03:50,027 --> 00:03:52,235
[Vocab] 会社

36
00:03:52,635 --> 00:03:58,180
[Host] It means a company or firm — the place people mean when they say they're heading in to work.

37
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:07,036
[Slow] 今、日本の会社は、ほかの国から買う方法を探しています。

38
00:04:07,836 --> 00:04:13,163
[Host] Right now, Japanese companies are searching for ways to buy from other countries.

39
00:04:13,764 --> 00:04:16,139
[Vocab] 探す

40
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:23,043
[Host] It means to look for or search for something — look for your keys, look for a job, look for a new supplier.

41
00:04:23,644 --> 00:04:31,420
[Slow] 同じ金属を、何度も使えるようにする研究も進んでいます。

42
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:37,475
[Host] Research on reusing the same metal again and again is also moving forward.

43
00:04:38,076 --> 00:04:40,451
[Vocab] 研究

44
00:04:40,851 --> 00:04:48,843
[Host] It means research or study — the careful digging into a question that scientists do. The person who does it is a researcher.

